WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.397 --> 00:00:02.350
- I'm waiting for death.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.550
- A baby.

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:04.752
- Love.

00:00:04.752 --> 00:00:08.540
(calm instrumental music)

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:11.400
- We're nurses, first of all,
so we're surrounded by it.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.100
But death not necessarily in a bad way,

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:18.070
just knowing that it happens to all of us,

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.100
and I like to remind myself every day

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.340
that I am going to die

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:27.347
and it makes me feel like
this is what I wanna do today,

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:32.453
hang out with my friends in a
park and I feel good about it.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:34.583
- A baby.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.020
I want to be pregnant with a baby.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:39.420
We had miscarriage a while ago,

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:41.880
so that's what I'm waiting for.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.580
I had a strange miscarriage.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:46.980
It was a partial mole,
so the fetus was alive

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.670
but it wasn't viable 'cause
it had 69 chromosomes,

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:51.190
and it was a silent miscarriage.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.740
And after that kind of pregnancy,

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.560
there is a chance for a
specific kind of cancer.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.060
So I'm like waiting for my blood tests

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.563
like over a course of months.

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:02.550
And I have two more months
and I'm in the clear.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:05.180
So I'm waiting. (chuckles)

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:06.653
- What am I waiting for?

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:09.000
That's a good question.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.940
Love, but I already have it. (laughs)

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.140
But I'm looking for more love

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:19.040
because that's the most important
thing in life, isn't it?

00:01:20.449 --> 00:01:21.610
That's right.

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:23.880
- That is such an open-ended question.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.930
Oh my god, it's so...

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:28.990
I could feel the gravity. (chuckles)

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:31.720
I guess I'm waiting for the
next big thing to happen,

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:33.050
whether it be love,

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:36.033
whether it be the next
big adventure that I take.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:38.933
It's hard to answer that.

00:01:38.933 --> 00:01:40.560
I guess it's like I'm
not waiting for anything.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:41.775
I'm just waiting.

00:01:41.775 --> 00:01:42.940
- [Thoraya] You listed a few things.

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:46.060
You said, "Whether it's love
when my next big adventure."

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:48.520
If it loves you, what
does it look like to you?

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:49.760
- It should feel comfortable.

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:51.410
It doesn't feel nervous,
it doesn't feel anxious.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:54.220
It just feels like you found a friend

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:56.470
that wants to stay with
you for like forever.

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:00.540
And yeah, it just feels
like you found a friend

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.050
that you wanna do life with.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.740
It's a loving partner, someone you just,

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:07.597
like anything you do in
your day you're just like,

00:02:07.597 --> 00:02:10.010
"Wow, I wish that person
could have it too."

00:02:10.010 --> 00:02:13.630
Or I wish we could bottle
it up and save it for them

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:15.190
so they could have if they're not there.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:17.840
I guess that's what love
is, like in its purest form.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.140
- I'm waiting for healing from people

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.073
who never healed themselves.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.513
- A better circumstance.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:34.440
- I'm waiting for the world to slow down.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:38.380
- Right now, I'm waiting to
go to college and start fresh,

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:39.880
and I'm really excited for it.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:41.690
- I don't know.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:45.357
I guess I'm waiting for
like the right moment.

00:02:46.753 --> 00:02:49.340
- I hope I'm not. (laughs)

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:53.230
Say I'd rather not wait
and do it now, I guess,

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.830
take the steps.

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:57.690
- I'm waiting to stop
being afraid of things.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:02.690
I'm afraid of new things
and change and myself.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.080
As much as I talk about
wanting to be more of myself,

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.190
it scares me to do that.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:11.970
So I guess I'm waiting for the day

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:14.780
that I actually feel I can do that.

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:17.720
And I don't know if it'll
be like some big event

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:20.680
or like if there'll
even be a big catalyst,

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:24.770
but I guess that's what I'm
waiting for, to be myself.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:27.700
- I am waiting for my super powers.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.100
Like when you read all those kid books,

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.230
like "Harry Potter," and
you're like, oh what,

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.327
they're 11, 12 when they were like,

00:03:33.327 --> 00:03:35.380
"Here's your letter to
Hogwarts," or something.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:36.810
But I feel like it's all those milestones,

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:40.227
like 13, 15, 16, like the 18.

00:03:40.227 --> 00:03:42.800
I'm like, well, I'm past all those stages

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.410
and I've not come in to any
power so I'm a little let down.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.400
But there's still time maybe.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.850
So I'll just keep holding out for it.

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:53.710
- That's a good one. (laughs)

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:58.740
You might wanna get his answer first.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:03:59.903
That was perfect.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.060
What are you waiting for?

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:02.987
- Cheese pizza.

00:04:02.987 --> 00:04:04.690
(people laughing)

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:06.110
- Andrew lives in the moment,

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:08.823
and the next moment planned is dinner.

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:12.550
- [Thoraya] That's a
great answer, honestly.

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:13.383
- Right?

00:04:13.383 --> 00:04:15.327
Like, of course, I have to think like,

00:04:15.327 --> 00:04:17.260
"Oh, what am I waiting for?"

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:20.142
- I'm waiting to buy him
and her the cheese pizza.

00:04:20.142 --> 00:04:23.264
(people laughing)

00:04:23.264 --> 00:04:26.847
(calm instrumental music)

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:31.700
- I think that it's really important

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:34.920
to have a really positive outlook on life.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:39.390
And I think that I'm waiting for myself

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:44.390
to get into my own
positive mindset and stop,

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:48.410
how do I say this,

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:53.410
and stop like blocking myself

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.713
from like, you know, achieving nirvana.

00:04:58.050 --> 00:04:59.870
- I feel like I'm always waiting

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:03.040
thinking that, like, I
have a better opportunity

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:05.860
to do things like...

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:08.020
In my head, I know exactly how I wanna be.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:10.300
I know things that I
don't wanna do anymore

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:13.590
and aspects of myself and
my being that I don't like

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:15.410
and that I really wanna change,

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.640
and subconsciously I
just continue to do it.

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:20.830
And then after the fact, I
realize I could have taken that

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:23.350
as an opportunity to change
in the way that I want to

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:25.570
and grow as a person.

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:27.697
And then I'm like,

00:05:27.697 --> 00:05:30.830
"Dammit, I have to take
the next opportunity."

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:35.243
And I just need to realize
it before I even do it.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:36.993
Yeah.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:41.703
- I think I'm just waiting to
like find peace within myself.

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:44.143
It's been a really hard year.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:47.040
I don't know whether it means, you know,

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:49.960
like be feeling confident in myself

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:51.900
or just kind of where I'm going in life.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:52.960
I'm going to college soon

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:55.670
and I kind of don't know what I'm doing.

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:57.190
It feels really lonely sometimes,

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:59.730
and just, you know, it's really hard

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:01.020
to find peace within yourself

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:04.330
and like feeling okay and confident

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.720
when, you know, you feel really alone,

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:11.720
and like finding outlets,
it's really tough sometimes,

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:16.180
especially when you don't have
parents' guidance, you know?

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:17.240
Yeah.

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:20.150
- I am waiting to...

00:06:21.923 --> 00:06:26.693
Yeah, I'm waiting to start my
life and I'm waiting for love.

00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:31.770
I'm not a very accepting person of love,

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:34.830
but I found it in someone
and I found it somewhere.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:36.930
Love isn't very easy in my family,

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:39.160
it's very reciprocated differently,

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:40.970
and I'm just trying to make sure

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:42.960
that I don't follow those footsteps.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:45.080
Watching my parents marriage,

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:47.423
that's not the way that
I want my love to be.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.350
I want it to be different and beautiful

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:55.350
and not full of disrespect
and unhealed trauma.

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:58.640
I wanna make sure that
I found my own self love

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:00.960
in a love with another person.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:03.683
- These are more wishes, I
guess you could say, but,

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:08.030
yeah, I think for financial stability,

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:11.560
which would then being able to
maybe eventually buy a house,

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:13.660
maybe be able to take vacations.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:15.590
But more importantly I feel
like it's more important

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:18.260
for everybody to be equal.

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:20.240
I feel like there's so many
people who don't have stuff

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:21.830
who work super hard for it,

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.150
and other people who work hard for it

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:26.103
but just get an exorbitant
amount of stuff.

00:07:26.103 --> 00:07:27.120
- [Child] And pick me up.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.660
- And pick you up.

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:32.520
And for this one to be healthy
for his entire life, right?

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:34.140
Yes.
(child laughing)

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:36.290
Oh, and since I'm a diabetic, I would love

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:40.573
to find cures instead of treatments.

00:07:41.921 --> 00:07:43.830
- I don't feel like I
wait a lot, to be honest.

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:45.590
Like, I've accomplished so many things

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:48.470
and every time I put my mind
on like towards something

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:49.680
I kind of do it.

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:53.840
So I don't really wait
on anything or anyone.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.490
I'm a professional skateboarder.

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:56.361
- [Thoraya] Oh no way!

00:07:56.361 --> 00:07:58.090
- I just got back from the Olympics,

00:07:58.090 --> 00:08:02.740
and, you know, I'm in San
Diego with my girlfriend

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:04.800
living life. (chuckles)

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:09.800
- I am waiting to find time
'cause, right, I have two jobs

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:12.330
and, of course, my family
just moved in with me

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:14.390
and so we're getting resettled

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:19.080
to go see my 100-year-old
mother because I love her

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:22.510
and she lives in Sacramento
so she's not real close.

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:26.770
And I never know when the last
time I'm gonna see her is,

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:30.000
and she taught me everything
that's important in life.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.870
And I love her so much.

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:33.660
And I was thinking about it today,

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:36.140
tomorrow she could be
gone, but she's so awesome.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:38.730
I'm a band and music teacher,

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:42.360
and I grew up learning music from her.

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:45.247
And my dad who had divorced, her said,

00:08:45.247 --> 00:08:47.480
"Oh, I want you to do something else."

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:48.313
But you know what?

00:08:48.313 --> 00:08:50.130
I am a band and music teacher.

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:52.720
And I make my living. I have two jobs.

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:55.760
I have a music studio
because my mom taught me

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.290
everything she knows.

00:08:57.290 --> 00:09:01.140
And I love, have a passion for
music, and I just miss her.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.350
So I'm waiting, I was
looking at the calendar,

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:06.540
I'm waiting to find a weekend
that I can just fly up

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:09.800
and just spend time with my dear mother

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:12.653
'cause I love her so much
and she's 100 years old.

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:17.400
- That's right really,
really good question.

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:18.963
Zoe, what am I waiting for?

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:21.770
I should just do it.

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:23.300
You know what? Don't wait for it.

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:24.583
Just do it.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:27.210
That's my answer.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:30.040
Now here for the first
time on your own channel,

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:31.450
you get it flipped around.

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:35.600
So Thoraya, tell us and
tell your dear viewers,

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:37.143
what are you waiting for?

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:43.130
- Well, I was just reminded
a bit by your answer.

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:45.400
You said you're a band teacher,

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:46.987
and my followers actually know this

00:09:46.987 --> 00:09:48.580
'cause I've said it before,

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:51.940
but I've been wanting to
start a band with my cousins.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:55.160
And I guess that's what
I've been waiting for.

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:56.730
I don't know what I'm waiting for, though.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:58.130
Like, I don't even know where to start.

00:09:58.130 --> 00:09:59.203
So I guess-

00:09:59.203 --> 00:10:01.610
- [Band Teacher] Get those
cousins and get in a one room

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:03.299
and start jamming.

00:10:03.299 --> 00:10:05.700
- (laughs) Is it really that simple?

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.880
- It is. My kids all play instruments.

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:10.190
We all sing and we just get together

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:12.140
and sometimes somebody
will pick up a guitar

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:14.800
and I run and get my flute and
she starts playing the piano.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:18.880
He grabs a mandolin and we just have fun

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.540
creating with music.

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:22.900
- Now, we will tell you in the beginning

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:25.470
there might be a lot of, as Mom puts it,

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:27.320
creative dissonance.

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:30.360
You know, a lot of sounds that
just don't sound quite right,

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:33.130
but that's part of the creative process.

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:35.847
You gotta say, "I'm
willing to make mistakes

00:10:35.847 --> 00:10:38.277
"in order to be willing to learn

00:10:38.277 --> 00:10:41.403
"and take that willing to
learn and have fun with it."

00:10:41.403 --> 00:10:42.730
Because it's all about having fun,

00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:44.680
and if you're not having fun with it,

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:46.130
why do you wanna do it.

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:49.240
- Like, it's genuinely just
'cause I just imagine myself

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:51.470
playing the drums and it
brings me so much joy.

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:53.320
- [Band Teacher] There
you go. Get some sticks.

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:55.560
You don't even have to have a real drum,

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:56.580
you can bang on anything.

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:58.200
I teach band all the time.

00:10:58.200 --> 00:10:59.280
- Do you teach drums?

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:00.113
- [Band Teacher] I do.

00:11:00.113 --> 00:11:02.455
I teach percussion as part of the band.

00:11:02.455 --> 00:11:04.053
- Do you do private lessons?

00:11:04.053 --> 00:11:05.006
(people laughing)

00:11:05.006 --> 00:11:05.839
- Oh-oh.
- I do everything.

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:08.710
- Okay, wow.

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:10.840
- [Band Teacher] Believe me, I
have taught hundreds of kids.

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:12.290
- [Interviewer] So the question is,

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:13.540
what are you waiting for?

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:16.410
- I don't know. I feel like...

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:18.728
Going back to what you
said, I just gotta do it.

00:11:18.728 --> 00:11:19.561
- You do.
- You just gotta do it.

00:11:19.561 --> 00:11:20.930
- Just do it.

00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:23.352
Viewers, just do it.

00:11:23.352 --> 00:11:25.410
Thoraya, just do it.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:28.817
- Thank you so much. Wow.
- Yeah, have a great day.

00:11:29.918 --> 00:11:33.501
(calm instrumental music)

